<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>

  <!-- Constrictor binding: a late Anomaly psychic ritual that calls up a gorge
       constrictor and leashes it. The bound constrictor never bursts anyone - it
       pumps them as big as they can go, lets go and is used again.
       Code: Rituals/PsychicRitualDef_RRBindConstrictor.cs, the leashed flag in
       Hediff_RRConstricted, JobDriver_RRApplyBoundConstrictor. -->

  <ResearchProjectDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Anomaly">
    <defName>RR_ConstrictorBinding</defName>
    <label>constrictor binding</label>
    <description>Perform a psychic ritual over a lure of twisted meat and a dark archotech shard to call a gorge constrictor up out of the ground - and bind it. A bound constrictor can be set on anyone to pump them full. It is leashed: it will never make anyone burst.</description>
    <tab>Anomaly</tab>
    <prerequisites>
      <li>SummonPitGate</li>
    </prerequisites>
    <knowledgeCost>90</knowledgeCost>
    <knowledgeCategory>Advanced</knowledgeCategory>
    <researchViewX>7.50</researchViewX>
    <researchViewY>1.30</researchViewY>
    <generalRules>
      <rulesStrings>
        <li>subject-&gt;constrictor binding</li>
        <li>subject_story-&gt;watched a gorge constrictor pump a raider until the shard in its back went dark</li>
        <li>subject_story-&gt;kept a fleshbeast as a pet for three days, until it wasn't one</li>
        <li>subject_story-&gt;read the feeding logs of a cult that bred worms in its cellars</li>
        <li>subject_gerund-&gt;binding gorge constrictors</li>
        <li>subject_gerund-&gt;leashing fleshbeasts</li>
      </rulesStrings>
    </generalRules>
  </ResearchProjectDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase" MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Anomaly">
    <defName>RR_ConstrictorLure</defName>
    <label>constrictor lure</label>
    <description>A heap of twisted meat wrapped around a dark archotech shard, still faintly warm. Offered in a constrictor binding ritual, it draws a gorge constrictor up out of the ground. It is useless otherwise.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Item/Special/RR_ConstrictorLure</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <soundInteract>Standard_Pickup</soundInteract>
    <soundDrop>Standard_Drop</soundDrop>
    <stackLimit>5</stackLimit>
    <healthAffectsPrice>false</healthAffectsPrice>
    <genericMarketSellable>false</genericMarketSellable>
    <resourceReadoutPriority>Middle</resourceReadoutPriority>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>80</MaxHitPoints>
      <MarketValue>550</MarketValue>
      <Mass>2</Mass>
      <Flammability>0.5</Flammability>
      <DeteriorationRate>2</DeteriorationRate>
      <Beauty>-8</Beauty>
      <WorkToMake>6000</WorkToMake>
    </statBases>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>Manufactured</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <recipeMaker>
      <researchPrerequisite>RR_ConstrictorBinding</researchPrerequisite>
      <recipeUsers>
        <li>BioferriteShaper</li>
      </recipeUsers>
      <skillRequirements>
        <Crafting>5</Crafting>
      </skillRequirements>
      <workSpeedStat>GeneralLaborSpeed</workSpeedStat>
      <workSkill>Crafting</workSkill>
      <effectWorking>ButcherFlesh</effectWorking>
      <soundWorking>Recipe_ButcherCorpseFlesh</soundWorking>
      <displayPriority>130</displayPriority>
    </recipeMaker>
    <costList>
      <Shard>1</Shard>
      <Meat_Twisted>100</Meat_Twisted>
    </costList>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Anomaly">
    <defName>RR_BoundConstrictor</defName>
    <label>bound gorge constrictor</label>
    <description>A gorge constrictor curled around the dark archotech shard in its back, cinched with bioferrite and leashed by a psychic ritual. It lies docile until someone sets it on a person.

It then wraps around them, forces its proboscis into their mouth and empties its load into them, shrinking as it goes. Its leash holds: it never makes anyone burst. It lets go once it is empty, or once they are as big as they can go.

An emptied constrictor is shrivelled and useless until it reswells: keep it in a constrictor vat and feed the vat. Outside a vat it slowly shrivels. It can be torn off early.</description>
    <thingClass>ThingWithComps</thingClass>
    <category>Item</category>
    <drawerType>MapMeshOnly</drawerType>
    <alwaysHaulable>true</alwaysHaulable>
    <selectable>true</selectable>
    <useHitPoints>false</useHitPoints>
    <pathCost>14</pathCost>
    <altitudeLayer>Item</altitudeLayer>
    <stackLimit>1</stackLimit>
    <tradeNeverStack>true</tradeNeverStack>
    <genericMarketSellable>false</genericMarketSellable>
    <resourceReadoutPriority>Middle</resourceReadoutPriority>
    <rotatable>false</rotatable>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Item/Special/RR_BoundConstrictor</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <soundInteract>Standard_Pickup</soundInteract>
    <soundDrop>Standard_Drop</soundDrop>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>1500</MarketValue>
      <Mass>6</Mass>
      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
      <DeteriorationRate>0</DeteriorationRate>
      <Beauty>-10</Beauty>
    </statBases>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>ItemsMisc</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <tickerType>Rare</tickerType>
    <comps>
      <!-- its load and mutations (Things/BoundConstrictorData.cs) -->
      <li Class="RimRound.Things.CompProperties_RRBoundConstrictor" />
      <li Class="CompProperties_Usable">
        <useJob>RR_ApplyBoundConstrictor</useJob>
        <useLabel>Set on someone</useLabel>
        <showUseGizmo>true</showUseGizmo>
      </li>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Targetable">
        <compClass>RimRound.Comps.Things.CompTargetable_RRBoundConstrictor</compClass>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </ThingDef>

  <JobDef>
    <defName>RR_ApplyBoundConstrictor</defName>
    <driverClass>RimRound.AI.JobDriver_RRApplyBoundConstrictor</driverClass>
    <reportString>setting the bound gorge constrictor on TargetB.</reportString>
    <casualInterruptible>false</casualInterruptible>
  </JobDef>

  <RimRound.Rituals.PsychicRitualDef_RRBindConstrictor MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Anomaly">
    <defName>RR_BindConstrictor</defName>
    <label>constrictor binding</label>
    <description>Offer a constrictor lure in a psychic ritual to call a gorge constrictor up out of the ground and bind it to the invoker's will. A bound constrictor can be set on anyone to pump them full, and it never makes anyone burst.\n\nIf the binding slips, the constrictor rises wild and hostile.</description>
    <iconPath>Things/Item/Special/RR_BoundConstrictor</iconPath>
    <researchPrerequisite>RR_ConstrictorBinding</researchPrerequisite>
    <outcomeDescription>With the current ritual quality, there is a {0} chance that the binding slips and the constrictor rises wild.</outcomeDescription>
    <hoursUntilOutcome>5</hoursUntilOutcome>
    <castableOnPocketMaps>false</castableOnPocketMaps>
    <layerWhitelist>
      <li>Surface</li>
    </layerWhitelist>
    <wildChanceFromQualityCurve>
      <points>
        <li>(0, 0.8)</li>
        <li>(0.5, 0.35)</li>
        <li>(0.8, 0.1)</li>
        <li>(1, 0.02)</li>
      </points>
    </wildChanceFromQualityCurve>
    <requiredOffering>
      <filter>
        <thingDefs>
          <li>RR_ConstrictorLure</li>
        </thingDefs>
      </filter>
      <count>1</count>
    </requiredOffering>
    <cooldownHours>720</cooldownHours>
    <chanterRole>ChanterAdvanced</chanterRole>
  </RimRound.Rituals.PsychicRitualDef_RRBindConstrictor>

</Defs>
